TAMLINUX DESKTOP SHELL

Product shell, host contract, and session services for Hyprland/Quickshell.
Plugin payloads live under plugins/ <plugins/README>.

Historical 2026-10-03 shell-proof check dumps and Omarchy-era proof narrative
were removed from this file in the 2026-10-31 docs prune; retrieve the full
pre-prune text with
git show 139b060a717573fb2740c0f5e3b5deb599a6aeff:desktop/README.md (see
<FILING-CARD.md>).


START MENU (0.5.10)

Right-click unused bar space, or press SUPER and right-click anywhere, to open
Start near the pointer. It exposes Quick Launch and Settings in one searchable
list. Occupied bar widgets retain their own right-click behavior. SUPER + ALT
+ right-drag resizes windows.

Settings offers Color Palette, Text Size, Background and Bar Position.
tam-menu toggle start opens the combined view; tam-menu toggle quicklaunch
remains available. See the approved plan <../docs/plans/start-menu.md>.


CONSOLE-FIRST STARTUP

Tamlinux boots through visible text progress to a text login. The optional
desktop starts when the signed-in user runs tam-desktop on a local foreground
console. There is no graphical login manager. See console-first-startup.md
<../docs/plans/console-first-startup.md>.


NAMES

The Tamlinux shell is one Quickshell configuration that draws the bar and
panels and runs session services. Host in this directory means the plugin host
contract in shell/host/ (registry, settings, popouts, IPC, compositor facade).
Elsewhere, host means the distribution the workstation package is installed
on.

Ported code was copied from Omarchy (MIT, notice kept), adapted to Tamlinux,
and is maintained here; headers say Ported from omarchy ….


HOST CONTRACT

Each output gets its own bar object from desktop/shell/host/BarApi.qml. Plugin
source is not copied into this directory.

  Call: foreground, fontFamily, position, urgent, barSize
  Who uses it: all plugins
  Host behavior: Top or bottom bar, horizontal, owned palette and type scale.

  Call: bar.screen.name
  Who uses it: weather, tides
  Host behavior: The output this bar was built for.

  Call: setting() / updateEntryInline
  Who uses it: clock
  Host behavior: Scalar writes for a registered id.

  Call: moduleWidgets
  Who uses it: workspaces
  Host behavior: Every live instance of that id, across outputs.

  Call: requestPopout / releasePopout
  Who uses it: keyboard, monitor, sysinfo, weather, tides, clock
  Host behavior: One open popup per output.

  Call: switchPanelFrom
  Who uses it: clock, weather, tides
  Host behavior: Opens the next widget on that output with open/close.

  Call: showTooltip / hideTooltip
  Who uses it: sysinfo, monitor, shared buttons
  Host behavior: Separate overlay; size follows TAMLINUX_UI_SCALE.

  Call: shell.summon / hide / toggle
  Who uses it: monitor
  Host behavior: Registered panel on the focused output.

  Call: compositor.* keyboard helpers
  Who uses it: keyboard layout widget
  Host behavior: From the Hyprland adapter.

  Call: pickAgent()
  Who uses it: agents
  Host behavior: $TAMLINUX_BIN/tam-agent --pick when actions are enabled.

  Call: openTerminal(program)
  Who uses it: sysinfo, menu
  Host behavior: Bounded program names only.

  Call: notify(text)
  Who uses it: weather
  Host behavior: Plain notice up to 512 characters when actions are enabled.

Tam.Commons and Tam.Ui supply shared types and tokens. There is no
execDetached. Plugins import Tam.Commons and Tam.Ui from their own trees.


COMPOSITOR CONTRACT

Shell UI reads desktop/shell/host/Compositor.qml. HyprlandAdapter.qml is the
only shell file that imports Quickshell.Hyprland or starts /usr/bin/hyprctl.
SwayAdapter.qml loads only when TAMLINUX_COMPOSITOR=sway.

Named actions (focusWorkspace, focusOutput, setDpms) record the request unless
TAMLINUX_COMPOSITOR_LIVE_ACTIONS=1. Protocol proof:

    python3 desktop/launch-protocol-proof


SESSION SERVICES

shell/host/Services.qml loads services named in TAMLINUX_SERVICES
(comma-separated). TAMLINUX_BAR=0 runs services without a bar.

  Service: notifications
  Role: Freedesktop notifications, DND, history

  Service: osd
  Role: Volume/brightness/status overlays

  Service: clipboard
  Role: Clipboard history picker

  Service: emojis
  Role: Emoji picker

  Service: imagepicker
  Role: Image carousel for pickers

  Service: reminders
  Role: Timed reminder cards

  Service: menu
  Role: Command menu / Start

  Service: background
  Role: Desktop background layer

  Service: polkit
  Role: Session polkit agent

  Service: media
  Role: MPRIS media keys

  Service: battery
  Role: Low-battery warning and power profiles

  Service: idle
  Role: Stay Awake / idle lock

  Service: theme
  Role: Palette apply without restarting the shell


LAYOUT

    desktop/
      shell/shell.qml
      shell/host/          # bar API, compositor facade, adapters
      shell/services/      # session services
      shell/modules/Tam/   # Commons and Ui
      plugins/             # fred.* payloads
      tests/


THEME

tam-shell theme reload applies validated colors to Tam.Commons. Import
Tam.Commons as Commons (unqualified Color can mean QtQuick's type). Headless
checks: python3 desktop/check-theme --quickshell /path/to/quickshell. Full
Tamarack design is a separate milestone (theme-system.md
<../docs/plans/theme-system.md>).

The daily session starter is shell/host/session_start.py. It builds plugin
entries from ~/.config/tamlinux/plugins/ and reads
~/.config/tamlinux/shell/{layout,settings}.json.
